# Local dev helper that creates a demo church with a KNOWN password
# (demo@churchflow.test / password123). Useful locally, never in a repo or
# on a server — a seeded account with a published password is a back door.
/dev-demo.php

# Single-purpose debugging scripts written while chasing a specific Blade
# compile error and a health-endpoint test failure. They bootstrap Laravel and
# poke at compiled views / run probes directly. Genuinely useful when the same
# class of problem recurs, but they are scratch, not part of the app — nothing
# under app/, routes/, tests/ or resources/ references them.
/dev-balance.php
/dev-lines.php
/dev-view.php
/dev-health-probe.php
# Deployment credentials (FTP/FTPS, database, SMTP). These are supplied at
# deploy time and must never enter the repository or a build artifact.
/churchflow-deployment-secrets.env
/*-deployment-secrets.env
